# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Human-only review paths
#
# CI cannot catch the failure modes here, so a green build is not evidence that
# these changes are safe. They need a person to look.
#
# - Dependency graph (lockfile, mobile package.json, native-deps.json): a JS-only
#   dependency change can silently re-key the Expo native module graph onto a
#   second React/react-native instance, which blanks native video and GIF
#   rendering on a real device while typecheck, tests, and the bundle all pass.
#   See docs/architecture/ADR-013-mobile-versioning-and-ota-updates.md.
#   apps/convex/package.json is in here for the same class of reason: its
#   react and react-dom pins are load-bearing despite apps/convex shipping no
#   React code. Dropping either one re-keys a second `convex` instance (which
#   silently empties the generated api/internal types) or skews react/react-dom
#   (which threw on every verification email in production while CI was green).
#   CLAUDE.md spells both out.
# - Auth: a regression locks people out or lets the wrong people in, and tests
#   assert the code's behaviour rather than the policy it should encode.
# - Billing / finance: moves real money. Wrong is expensive and hard to unwind.
# - Migrations: run once against production data. There is no second attempt.
#
# NOTE: last matching pattern wins in CODEOWNERS, so these override the
# defaults above.
#
# This is reviewer routing and documentation, NOT a merge gate. Do not turn on
# "Require review from Code Owners" for these paths: @lilseyi is the only human
# here, and GitHub does not count a PR author's own review, so the toggle would
# make his own lockfile bumps and migrations unmergeable without an admin
# override. The real gate is that only lilseyi merges these, which the agent
# deny-rules in .claude/settings.json already enforce from the other side.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Dependency graph / native safety (ADR-013)
/pnpm-lock.yaml @lilseyi
/apps/mobile/package.json @lilseyi
/apps/mobile/native-deps.json @lilseyi
/apps/convex/package.json @lilseyi

# Auth - the directory plus the central modules that live outside it
/apps/convex/functions/auth/ @lilseyi
/apps/convex/auth.ts @lilseyi
/apps/convex/lib/auth.ts @lilseyi
/apps/convex/functions/authInternal.ts @lilseyi

# Billing, payments, and the money ledger
/apps/convex/functions/billing.ts @lilseyi
/apps/convex/functions/ee/billing.ts @lilseyi
/apps/convex/functions/finance/ @lilseyi
/apps/convex/lib/finance/ @lilseyi

# Migrations - run once against production data
# (a trailing-slash pattern does not match a sibling FILE of the same name, so
# every migrations.ts is listed explicitly)
/apps/convex/migrations/ @lilseyi
/apps/convex/functions/migrations/ @lilseyi
/apps/convex/functions/migrations.ts @lilseyi
